      "writtenOn": "2020-06-02T11:04:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I noticed that current core/riscv-rv32i doesn\u0027t check return value of chip_get_ec_int().  When the return value is not okay, it just screws up the core and panics.\n\nI think we could fix core/riscv-rv32i to check the return value.  Define (-1) as the designated error code.\n\nI would like to keep it as is (0 is not okay for current Asurada SCP) and submit another patch for fixing the core/riscv-rv32i and this.\n\nNo further prints are needed here.  Because it panics and core/riscv-rv32i already has some printing functions for that (core/riscv-rv32i/panic.c).",
      "parentUuid": "2cf8f4a7_85d772ca",
